From a6e51c9ce17924fb08742f03f0418e0636490363 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yibo Wang <2024312277@stu.hit.edu.cn>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 10:12:06 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: iris: Kaanapali (VPU4) video codec support for
 iceland

Backport two upstream series plus one vendor-tree patch, all verified
on the device with hardware H.264/HEVC/VP9 decode (NV12/P010/UBWC
output) and H.264/HEVC encode:

- upstream v3 'iris: Migrate iommus to iris sub nodes' patches 01-07
  (bindings, of_iommu iommu-ranges reserved-region derivation, context
  bank child devices, buffer routing, DMA-mask guard); 08-13 are other
  SoC dts updates and were not needed.
- upstream v4 'iris: add support for kaanapali platform' with local
  deltas: .firmware_desc_gen2 renamed to .firmware_desc (7.2 has no
  gen1/gen2 split), and the mtp enablement patch replaced by the
  iceland node using the vendor vpu40_2v.mbn firmware (SoC rev 2.0).
- sm8750-video-accel VA-API patch (decode-order / loop filter
  controls), two hunks re-done by hand plus the missing
  iris_set_deblock_gen2 prototype restored.

Patch provenance and local deltas documented in
repos/iris-kaanapali-patches/README.md (outside this tree).

Device: 2000000.video-codec probes with pixel/non-pixel context
banks, runtime suspend resumes clean (vpu4 power-off sequence), no
SMMU faults or LPI timeouts.
